{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":4165882,"ns":0,"title":"Convex geometry","extract":"In mathematics, convex geometry is the branch of geometry studying convex sets, mainly in Euclidean space. Convex sets occur naturally in many areas: computational geometry, convex analysis, discrete geometry, functional analysis, geometry of numbers, integral geometry, linear programming, probability theory, game theory, etc.","description":"Branch of geometry","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}